Screen 3: Register New Product Form
A professional product registration screen for the SmartShelf inventory platform featuring a structured two-column layout: an input form on the left and a live real-time preview card on the right. Desktop web application, Inter font, zero emojis.

DESIGN SYSTEM (REQUIRED):
- Platform: Desktop Web SaaS
- Colors: White (#ffffff) form panels, slate borders (#e2e8f0), cobalt primary button (#1d4ed8)
- Typography: Inter, 500-weight field labels, crisp validation states

Page Structure:
1. Sidebar: "SmartShelf" navigation with "Add Product" highlighted as active.
2. Page Header:
   - Title: "Register New Product"
   - Subtitle: "Enter product metadata, stock counts, valuation, and shelf life parameters."

3. Two-Column Form Layout:
   - Left Column (60% width - Input Form):
     * Section 1: "Product Details"
       - Product Name input field with placeholder "e.g. Arabica Roast Coffee Beans 500g" (required).
       - Category selection: Toggle between "Select Existing Category" dropdown (Dairy, Beverages, Pantry, Bakery) and "Create New Category" text field.
       - SKU Barcode field with generate button.
     * Section 2: "Inventory & Pricing"
       - Quantity On Hand numeric stepper (default: 10, min: 0).
       - Unit Cost (Rs) currency field with prefix "Rs" (default: 150.00).
       - Real-time calculated batch valuation display.
     * Section 3: "Lifecycle & Thresholds"
       - Toggle switch: "Enable Expiration Tracking".
       - Expiry Date picker (calendar control, disabled if tracking is toggled off).
       - Minimum Stock Alert Threshold input (default: 5 units).
     * Action Footer:
       - "Cancel / Reset" secondary gray button.
       - "Register Product" primary blue button (#1d4ed8).

   - Right Column (40% width - Real-Time Card Preview):
     * Card Header: "Real-Time Card Preview" with caption "This is how this product will appear in the catalog."
     * Preview Card Component:
       - Top: Badge with category name and stock health indicator ("In Stock" pill).
       - Middle: Bold product title, SKU ID tag, and unit pricing display.
       - Key Metrics row: Stock Volume, Unit Price, Batch Valuation.
       - Expiry Status row: Expiry date with countdown meter or "Non-perishable".
       - Minimum Threshold indicator: "Alert triggers when stock drops to 5 units".

